    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "RHEL-10-200621 - RHEL 10 must use the common access card (CAC) smart card driver."
      info        : "Smart card login provides two-factor authentication stronger than that provided by a username and password combination. Smart cards leverage public key infrastructure to provide and verify credentials. Configuring the smart card driver helps to prevent the use of unauthorized smart cards.

Satisfies: SRG-OS-000104-GPOS-00051, SRG-OS-000106-GPOS-00053, SRG-OS-000107-GPOS-00054, SRG-OS-000109-GPOS-00056, SRG-OS-000108-GPOS-00055"
      solution    : "Configure RHEL 10 to load the CAC driver:

$ sudo opensc-tool --set-conf-entry app:default:card_drivers:cac

