    <custom_item>
      type        : RPM_CHECK
      description : "RHEL-10-200690 - RHEL 10 must notify designated personnel if baseline configurations are changed in an unauthorized manner."
      info        : "The \"postfix\" package provides the mail command required to allow sending email notifications of unauthorized configuration changes to designated personnel."
      solution    : "Configure RHEL 10 to notify designated personnel if baseline configurations are changed in an unauthorized manner.

Install the postfix package with the following command:

$ sudo dnf -y install postfix"
      reference   : "800-171|3.3.4,800-171r3|03.03.04a.,800-53|AU-5a.,800-53r5|AU-5a.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000139,CN-L3|7.1.3.3(e),CSF|PR.PT-1,DISA_Benchmark|RHEL_10_STIG,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(b),ITSG-33|AU-5a.,NESA|T3.6.2,QCSC-v1|8.2.1,QCSC-v1|13.2,Rule-ID|SV-280997r1195387_rule,STIG-ID|RHEL-10-200690,Vuln-ID|V-280997"
