    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "RHEL-10-400230 - RHEL 10 must be configured to prohibit modification of permissions for cron configuration files and directories from the operating system defaults."
      info        : "If the permissions of cron configuration files or directories are modified from the operating system defaults, it may be possible for individuals to insert unauthorized cron jobs that perform unauthorized actions, including potentially escalating privileges."
      solution    : "Configure RHEL 10 to prohibit modification of permissions for cron configuration files and directories from the operating system defaults with the following commands:

$ sudo dnf reinstall cronie crontabs
$ rpm --setugids cronie crontabs
$ rpm --setperms cronie crontabs"
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.6,800-171|3.4.7,800-171r3|03.04.06a.,800-53|CM-7a.,800-53r5|CM-7a.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000381,CN-L3|7.1.3.5(c),CN-L3|8.1.4.4(a),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF|PR.PT-3,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,DISA_Benchmark|RHEL_10_STIG,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|CM-7a.,NIAv2|SS15a,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.1,PCI-DSSv4.0|2.2.3,QCSC-v1|3.2,Rule-ID|SV-281063r1195403_rule,STIG-ID|RHEL-10-400230,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-281063"
      see_also    : "https://dl.dod.cyber.mil/wp-content/uploads/stigs/zip/U_RHEL_10_V1R2_STIG.zip"
      cmd         : "/bin/rpm --verify cronie crontabs | /bin/awk '! ($2 == \"c\" && $1 ~ /^.\\..\\.\\.\\.\\..\\./) {print $0}' | /bin/awk '{print} END {if (NR == 0) print \"pass\"; else print \"fail\"}'"
      expect      : "^pass$"
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "RHEL-10-400235 - RHEL 10 must enforce mode \"0740\" or less permissive for local initialization files."
      info        : "Local initialization files are used to configure the user's shell environment upon login. Malicious modification of these files could compromise accounts upon login."
      solution    : "Configure RHEL 10 so that all local initialization files have a mode of \"0740\" or less permissive with the following command:

Note: The example will be for the \"disauser\" user, who has a home directory of \"/home/disauser\".

$ sudo chmod 0740 /home/disauser/.<INIT_FILE>"
      reference   : "800-171|3.1.1,800-171r3|03.01.02,800-53|AC-3,800-53r5|AC-3,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000213,CN-L3|8.1.4.2(f),CN-L3|8.1.4.11(b),CN-L3|8.1.10.2(c),CN-L3|8.5.3.1,CN-L3|8.5.4.1(a),CSF|PR.AC-4,CSF|PR.PT-3,CSF2.0|PR.AA-05,CSF2.0|PR.DS-10,CSF2.0|PR.IR-01,DISA_Benchmark|RHEL_10_STIG,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.5.15,ISO-27001-2022|A.5.33,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.3,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.18,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.20,ISO/IEC-27001|A.9.4.1,ISO/IEC-27001|A.9.4.5,ITSG-33|AC-3,NESA|T4.2.1,NESA|T5.4.4,NESA|T5.4.5,NESA|T5.5.4,NESA|T5.6.1,NESA|T7.5.2,NESA|T7.5.3,NIAv2|AM3,NIAv2|SS29,QCSC-v1|3.2,QCSC-v1|5.2.2,QCSC-v1|13.2,Rule-ID|SV-281064r1165547_rule,STIG-ID|RHEL-10-400235,TBA-FIISB|31.1,Vuln-ID|V-281064"
      see_also    : "https://dl.dod.cyber.mil/wp-content/uploads/stigs/zip/U_RHEL_10_V1R2_STIG.zip"
      cmd         : "/bin/awk -F: '($3 == 0 || $3 > 999) && $3 != 65534 { print $6 }' /etc/passwd | /bin/sort -u | while read D; do /bin/stat -c '%F:%a:%A %n' $D/.[!.]* 2>/dev/null; done | /bin/awk -F: '$1 !~ /directory/ && $2 !~ /^[01234567][04][0]$/ { print $3; n+=1 } END { if (n<1) print \"none\" }'"
      expect      : "^none$"
    </custom_item>

    <item>
      description      : "RHEL-10-400240 - RHEL 10 must enforce mode \"0750\" or less permissive for local interactive user home directories."
      info             : "Excessive permissions on local interactive user home directories may allow unauthorized access to user files by other users."
      solution         : "Configure RHEL 10 so that the mode of interactive user's home directories is set to \"0750\".

To change the mode of a local interactive user's home directory, use the following command:

Note: The example will be for the user \"disauser\".

$ sudo chmod 0750 /home/disauser"
