      file        : "/etc/pam.d/sudo"
      regex       : "pam_succeed_if"
      expect      : "pam_succeed_if"
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK_NOT
      description : "RHEL-10-600520 - RHEL 10 must restrict privilege elevation to authorized personnel."
      info        : "If the \"sudoers\" file is not configured correctly, any user defined on the system can initiate privileged actions on the target system."
      solution    : "Configure RHEL 10 to restrict privilege elevation to authorized personnel.

Remove the following entries from the \"/etc/sudoers\" file or configuration file under \"/etc/sudoers.d/\":

ALL ALL=(ALL) ALL
ALL ALL=(ALL:ALL) ALL"
      reference   : "800-53|SI-6a.,800-53r5|SI-6a.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-002696,DISA_Benchmark|RHEL_10_STIG,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|SI-6a.,Rule-ID|SV-281207r1166573_rule,STIG-ID|RHEL-10-600520,Vuln-ID|V-281207"
      see_also    : "https://dl.dod.cyber.mil/wp-content/uploads/stigs/zip/U_RHEL_10_V1R2_STIG.zip"
      file        : "/etc/sudoers /etc/sudoers.d/*"
      regex       : "^[\\s]*ALL[\\s]+"
      expect      : "^[\\s]*ALL[\\s]+ALL=\\(ALL(:ALL)?\\)[\\s]+ALL"
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK_NOT
      description : "RHEL-10-600530 - RHEL 10 must require users to reauthenticate for privilege escalation."
      info        : "Without reauthentication, users may access resources or perform tasks for which they do not have authorization.

When operating systems provide the capability to escalate a functional capability, it is critical that the user reauthenticate.

Satisfies: SRG-OS-000373-GPOS-00156, SRG-OS-000373-GPOS-00157, SRG-OS-000373-GPOS-00158"
      solution    : "Configure RHEL 10 to not allow users to execute privileged actions without authenticating.

Remove any occurrence of \"!authenticate\" found in the \"/etc/sudoers\" file or files in the \"/etc/sudoers.d\" directory:

$ sudo sed -i '/\\!authenticate/ s/^/# /g' /etc/sudoers /etc/sudoers.d/*"
      reference   : "800-171r3|03.05.01b.,800-53|IA-11,800-53r5|IA-11,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-002038,CSF|PR.AC-1,CSF2.0|PR.AA-01,CSF2.0|PR.AA-03,DISA_Benchmark|RHEL_10_STIG,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(d),QCSC-v1|13.2,Rule-ID|SV-281208r1166576_rule,STIG-ID|RHEL-10-600530,Vuln-ID|V-281208"
      see_also    : "https://dl.dod.cyber.mil/wp-content/uploads/stigs/zip/U_RHEL_10_V1R2_STIG.zip"
      file        : "/etc/sudoers /etc/sudoers.d/*"
      regex       : "!authenticate"
      expect      : "!authenticate"
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type            : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
      description     : "RHEL-10-600540 - RHEL 10 must require reauthentication when using the \"sudo\" command."
      info            : "Without reauthentication, users may access resources or perform tasks for which they do not have authorization.

When operating systems provide the capability to escalate a functional capability, it is critical that the organization requires the user to reauthenticate when using the \"sudo\" command.

If the value is set to an integer less than \"0\", the user's time stamp will not expire, and the user will not have to reauthenticate for privileged actions until the user's session is terminated.

Satisfies: SRG-OS-000373-GPOS-00156, SRG-OS-000373-GPOS-00157, SRG-OS-000373-GPOS-00158"
      solution        : "Configure RHEL 10 to reauthenticate \"sudo\" commands after the specified timeout.

Add the following line to \"/etc/sudoers\" or a file in \"/etc/sudoers.d\":

Defaults timestamp_timeout=0"
      reference       : "800-171r3|03.05.01b.,800-53|IA-11,800-53r5|IA-11,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-002038,CSF|PR.AC-1,CSF2.0|PR.AA-01,CSF2.0|PR.AA-03,DISA_Benchmark|RHEL_10_STIG,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(d),QCSC-v1|13.2,Rule-ID|SV-281209r1166579_rule,STIG-ID|RHEL-10-600540,Vuln-ID|V-281209"
      see_also        : "https://dl.dod.cyber.mil/wp-content/uploads/stigs/zip/U_RHEL_10_V1R2_STIG.zip"
      file            : "/etc/sudoers /etc/sudoers.d/*"
      regex           : "timestamp_timeout"
      expect          : "^[\\s]*Defaults[\\s]+timestamp_timeout[\\s]*=[\\s]*[0-9]+"
      file_required   : NO
      min_occurrences : "1"
      string_required : NO
    </custom_item>

    <if>
      <condition auto:"FAILED" type:"AND">
        <custom_item>
          type            : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
          description     : "rootpw"
