    <custom_item>
      type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
      description : "RHEL-10-700120 - RHEL 10 must mount \"/boot\" with the \"nodev\" option."
      info        : "The only legitimate location for device files is the \"/dev\" directory located on the root partition. The only exception to this is chroot jails."
      solution    : "Configure RHEL 10 to mount \"/boot\" with the \"nodev\" option.

Modify \"/etc/fstab\" to use the \"nodev\" option on the \"/boot\" directory.

To reload all implicit mount units and update the dependency graph so that new options will apply correctly at next remount, run the following command:

$ sudo systemctl daemon-reload

Use the following command to apply the changes immediately without a reboot:

$ sudo mount -o remount /boot"
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.7,800-171r3|03.04.06,800-53|CM-7(2),800-53r5|CM-7(2),CAT|II,CCI|CCI-001764,CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF|PR.PT-3,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,DISA_Benchmark|RHEL_10_STIG,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|CM-7(2),NIAv2|SS15a,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.2,QCSC-v1|3.2,Rule-ID|SV-281232r1166648_rule,STIG-ID|RHEL-10-700120,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-281232"
      see_also    : "https://dl.dod.cyber.mil/wp-content/uploads/stigs/zip/U_RHEL_10_V1R2_STIG.zip"
      file        : "/etc/fstab"
      regex       : "^[^#\\n\\r]+[\\s]+/boot[\\s]+[^#\\n\\r]+nodev"
      expect      : "^[^#\\n\\r]+[\\s]+/boot[\\s]+[^#\\n\\r]+nodev"
    </custom_item>

