        <custom_item>
          type        : CMD_EXEC
          description : "Verify that the kdump service is masked with the following command for UnitFileState"
          cmd         : "/bin/systemctl show kdump | /bin/grep \"UnitFileState\""
          expect      : "^[\\s]*UnitFileState[\\s]*=[\\s]*masked[\\s]*$"
        </custom_item>

        <custom_item>
          type        : CMD_EXEC
          description : "Verify that the kdump service is masked with the following command for LoadState"
          cmd         : "/bin/systemctl show kdump | /bin/grep \"LoadState\""
          expect      : "^[\\s]*LoadState[\\s]*=[\\s]*masked[\\s]*$"
        </custom_item>

        <custom_item>
          type        : CMD_EXEC
          description : "Verify that the kdump service is disabled in system boot configuration"
          cmd         : "/bin/systemctl is-enabled kdump"
          expect      : "^[\\s]*(disabled|masked)[\\s]*$"
        </custom_item>

        <custom_item>
          type        : CMD_EXEC
          description : "Verify that the kdump service is not active"
          cmd         : "/bin/systemctl is-active kdump"
          expect      : "^[\\s]*(inactive|failed)[\\s]*$"
        </custom_item>
      </condition>

      <then>
        <report type:"PASSED">
          description : "RHEL-10-701200 - RHEL 10 must disable the kdump service."
          info        : "Kernel core dumps may contain the full contents of system memory at the time of the crash. Kernel core dumps consume a considerable amount of disk space and may result in denial of service by exhausting the available space on the target file system partition. Unless the system is used for kernel development or testing, there is little need to run the kdump service."
          solution    : "Configure RHEL 10 to disable and mask the kdump service.

To disable the kdump service, run the following command:

$ sudo systemctl disable --now kdump
Removed '/etc/systemd/system/multi-user.target.wants/kdump.service'.

To mask the kdump service, run the following command:

$ sudo systemctl mask --now kdump
Created symlink '/etc/systemd/system/kdump.service' ? '/dev/null'."
